  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Westwater is advancing a pre-revenue, vertically integrated graphite platform in Alabama, aiming to serve the battery anode supply chain at a time when U.S. overdependence on Chinese graphite creates a strong geopolitical tailwind. The company remains in the permitting and construction phase, with no commercial production, so its investment narrative is tied entirely to the promise of a future domestic supply chain rather than current market traction. End-market demand signals from electrification are supportive, but the business is still de-risking its permitting path and customer qualification efforts.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is focused on deliberate, milestone-driven execution: progressing Coosa mine permitting, customer qualification activities, and measured construction at the Kellyton processing plant, while actively pursuing external financing including a potential EXIM loan. The strategy centers on bringing a fully domestic, mine-to-market operation online, but the narrative remains contingent on securing funding and regulatory approvals. The tone is one of cautious advancement, with the market closely watching whether the team can convert strategic intent into operational reality amid substantial execution uncertainty.",
